# No noise / placeholder Desktop icons (hard rule)

Operator defect (2026-08): Desktop **Jump Config** showed a **multi-colored
noise/static** icon (plus the UAC shield). Recurrence (2026-08-06): `mix-server`
WiX shipped **BMP/DIB-only** product ICOs (~285 KB) that Explorer can paint as
static; the local tree had drifted from the PNG-compressed `core-assets`
installer-shortcuts. That class of failure is forbidden permanently — not a
Windows quirk to ignore.

## The rule

> **Never generate, commit, stage, sync, or ship Desktop, Start Menu,
> Add/Remove Programs, WiX `Icon=`, or PE-embedded icons that are random-bit /
> noise / static pixels, or that are BMP/DIB-only `.ico` files. Every advertised
> shortcut and every shipping PE / MSI icon resource MUST be a PNG-compressed
> AIC `.ico` produced in `core-assets` (or a validated `installer-shortcuts`
> derivative) and copied into consumers via `sync-to-projects.ps1`. Agents MUST
> NOT invent, regenerate, or "fix" icons with ad-hoc ImageMagick / `tauri icon`
> / hand edits outside `core-assets`.**

## Permanent generation ban (agents)

Forbidden in every repo under `c:\analog-pim`:

1. **Creating a new `.ico` outside `core-assets`** for product / shortcut / WiX
   / Tauri use.
2. **`magick … out.ico`** (or equivalent) emitting **BMP/DIB-only** frames —
   ImageMagick 7.1's default ICO path. Explorer paints those as multi-colored
   static even when the pixel art is a real logo.
3. **Committing an `.ico` with zero PNG payloads** (all frames
   `BITMAPINFOHEADER` / DIB). Size heuristic: a 256× multi-size tile around
   200–300 KB with no `89 50 4E 47` markers is almost always this defect.
4. **Using `aic-header.PLACEHOLDER-do-not-use.png`** or any random-bit bitmap as
   an icon or header source.
5. **Leaving shortcut `IconLocation` empty / `,0`** so Explorer falls back to a
   PE that embeds a bad or BMP-only ICO.

A new size or product variant is generated **inside `core-assets`**, committed
there, added to `sync-to-projects.ps1`, synced, then committed in each consumer.
See [`branding-assets.mdc`](branding-assets.mdc).

## Why shortcuts become noise

| Cause | What happens |
| --- | --- |
| **Shortcut `IconLocation` empty / `,0`** | Explorer extracts the target EXE's icon resource; a bad Tauri `icon.ico` makes the tile noise (+ UAC shield when elevated) |
| **Stale `src-tauri/icons/icon.ico`** | Historical `tauri icon` / unsynced tree left a noise ICO in Jump / DB Mgmt / WA / Recording / sibling Tauri apps; an empty `core-assets/icons/tauri` makes the sync a no-op |
| **BMP/DIB-only `.ico`** | Explorer paints BMP frames as multi-colored static; canonical generators assemble **PNG-compressed** ICO only |
| **Missing staged `aic-icon.ico`** | Side-load / incomplete MSI has the Tauri EXE but no sidecar icon; scripts omitting `IconLocation` fall back to the EXE |
| **Header / in-app placeholder** | `aic-header.PLACEHOLDER-do-not-use.png` must never re-enter `src/assets/` or be used as an icon source |
| **WiX / Mix drift** | `mix-server/wix/assets/aic-server-*.ico` must stay byte-identical to `core-assets/icons/desktop/installer-shortcuts/` via sync — never re-encode locally |

## Required patterns

1. **Canonical mark** — `core-assets/icons/desktop/aic-icon.ico` (or
   `icons/desktop/installer-shortcuts/*.ico` for MSI / WiX variants).
2. **PNG-compressed ICO** — at least one PNG payload per file (`89 50 4E 47`
   inside the `.ico`). Refuse BMP/DIB-only at stage time
   (`Stage-InstallerShortcutIcons.ps1`, Jump/DB/Recording/WA MSI builders, and
   any Mix / WiX asset copy).
3. **Shortcut `IconLocation`** — every Desktop / Start Menu `.lnk` for a
   configurator sets `IconLocation = "<installDir>\aic-icon.ico,0"` (or the
   WiX-advertised `Icon=` resource). Never rely on bare EXE `,0` for suite
   products.
4. **Tauri PE resources** — `src-tauri/icons/` comes from
   `core-assets/icons/tauri` via `sync-to-projects.ps1`. If that tree is empty,
   regenerate with
   `cargo tauri icon icons/source/aic-icon-1024.png --output icons/tauri`
   **in core-assets**, commit, sync — do not invent local noise ICOs.
5. **Pre-commit check (agents)** — before committing any `.ico` change verify:
   (a) the file is a `sync-to-projects.ps1` destination or the `core-assets`
   source itself; (b) at least one PNG frame exists; (c) SHA-256 matches the
   `core-assets` source when the path is a sync destination. If (b) or (c)
   fails, **do not commit**.
6. **Section 508 / credibility** — the brand image must be the real AIC mark
   ([`enterprise-compliance.mdc`](enterprise-compliance.mdc) §2;
   [`operator-ui-credibility.mdc`](operator-ui-credibility.mdc)).

## Forbidden constructs

- `New-Object WScript.Shell` / WiX `<Shortcut>` without an explicit AIC icon path
  or `Icon="ProductIcon"` backed by staged `aic-icon.ico`.
- Committing or syncing `aic-header.PLACEHOLDER-do-not-use.png` (or any
  random-bit bitmap) as `icon.ico`, `aic-icon.ico`, or header art.
- `magick … out.ico` without the PNG-compressed assembly path documented in
  `core-assets/icons/desktop/installer-shortcuts/README.md`.
- Replacing a sync-destination `.ico` with a locally regenerated file that does
  not match `core-assets` SHA-256.
- Claiming a Desktop icon fix without a screenshot of the live shortcut tile (or
  an extracted PNG from the shortcut's `IconLocation` target).

## Worked example

**Broken (Jump Config, 2026-08):** `Jump Config.lnk` →
`…\pim-jump-server-configurator-tauri.exe` with `IconLocation = ,0`; install dir
missing `aic-icon.ico`; the EXE embeds a noise `icon.ico`.

**Fixed:** stage `core-assets/icons/desktop/aic-icon.ico` as
`%ProgramFiles%\AIC\PimJumpServer\aic-icon.ico`; set the shortcut
`IconLocation` to that file; keep `src-tauri/icons` synced from
`core-assets/icons/tauri`.

Same shape for the 2026-08-06 Mix WiX regression: ~285 KB BMP/DIB-only product
ICOs were restored from the byte-identical PNG-compressed
`core-assets/icons/desktop/installer-shortcuts/` copies (~14–16 KB) rather than
re-encoded in `mix-server`.

